@tradition late-piano
// Late piano (weekly, seat 15). The Captain plays the music-room piano on Thursday nights (her musician habit already);
// a few listen. Starts at 21:45, after the quiz on Deck 3 ends, so it's on another deck and never at the same time.
// Small and quiet on purpose: few go. Design note: plans/trad-notes-weekly.md.
k: 438
title: Late piano
when: weekly wednesday,thursday
at: 21:45-22:30
min: 20
jitter: 10
where: 4 pool music
hold: 1
who: marrow always, music 55%, musician 40%, night-owl 25%, everyone 4%
anim: marrow play, everyone none
host: marrow
from: The music room
invite: host=marrow odds=10% line="I'll be at the piano later. Come and listen, if you like. I take requests. Sometimes."

== mail
- Late piano tomorrow, {time} in the music room, Deck 4. The Captain plays; anyone may listen. Quiet voices, please.

== ask
- The Captain's playing tonight, late. I'll be in the music room.
- Late piano tonight. I always mean to go to bed early. I never do.   #funny
- Going to hear the Captain play later. It's the calmest hour of the week.   #warm

== here
- Shh. This is the slow one.
- Listen to that. Who knew?   #warm
- I don't know what it's called. I just like it.

== thanks
- You slip into the music room and sit with the listeners. The Captain plays something slow and doesn't look up.   #warm

== chatter
- The Captain played something new last night. Nobody asked what it was.   #warm
- I didn't know the Captain could play until my first Thursday aboard.
- Late piano is the only time the Captain looks off duty.
